-- `src/agent.js` + `src/glow.js`: the agent globe (Strands), bottom centre, and an Apple Intelligence-style activation: a
-  WebGL edge glow (bright rim + soft flowing bloom on the screen's rounded edges) ripples in with a small scene bounce,
-  then fades; it is held while the agent works or listens. The globe's menu holds Notebook, Settings, Read as text,
-  Review sources and Hide/Show the conversation.
-- `src/main.js`: the state machine for P00-P14, the save system, the subtitles and the actions.
-- HUD: nothing on screen but the room and the globe. The agent speaks in subtitles beside the globe; choices are plain
-  text options under the line. In the held case file the only marks are two stamps against the page edge
-  (Foundations, Set aside; shown on hover, always on touch) and a page count. Keys: arrows turn, F/S stamp, Esc puts
-  the file down. Filters live on the Review page (P04). Content cards and dialogs share the globe menu's dark glass:
-  centred for the Review list and the debrief, top right (beside the subtitles) for headlines, the response package and
-  the topic check. Options are "›" text; the one main action in a dialog is a white pill.
+Models are copied from `../blender/production/export/` by `npm run assets`. `public/models`, `public/draco`, `dist` and `node_modules` are regenerated locally and intentionally excluded from this handoff ZIP. Keep this folder beside `app/` and `blender/`; do not move it out of the kit.
 
